	(text "Click a box on the left to open its page. \"Contents\" and the page numbers at the bottom right of\nevery page lead back here and to each page.\n\nCyan lines are connections: wires and pin ends, all one width. A dot joins lines; a cross on a pin\nend means the pin is not connected. Pins connect by net labels (the boxed names): pins whose labels\ncarry the same name are on one net, on any page. [3/C4] after a label: page 3 carries that net too,\nits label in zone C4 (column 4, row C of the border). Click it to land on that label. No\n[page/zone]: the net is on this page only. Click a part's reference to find its row in the parts\nlist; the row's page/zone leads back. White: parts and their references. Grey: values, pin names,\npin numbers. A dashed frame is a block of the circuit, titled at its top left. An amber K5 marks a\nKleidos addition or correction: it leads to its row below."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 215.9 45.085 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.75 1.75)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "dc9f4a28-f59f-5f0e-b0e4-7739c2a93cd5")
	)
	(text "Notes"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 215.9 84.16 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ebc12e11-1305-54e6-a05c-84ebf5baeb0f")
	)
	(text "Every part, pin and net of the M5StickC Plus 1.1, with the values the vendor documents: connectivity\ndocumented from the vendor's public documentation, with Kleidos additions and corrections listed on\npage 1 (M5Stack's StickC-Plus K016-P schematic, one page, Altium export of 2025-11-04, and its docs\npage, cited in README.md and netlist.yaml beside this file). Layout and symbols are this project's.\nNo footprints, no PCB, no part numbers beyond the documented ones. Values are as the vendor prints\nthem (5.1K, 100uF/4V). The schematic documents no part as not fitted, so no part carries a DNP mark.\nReference designators are the vendor's, not renumbered. Two parts carry none in the print and take\nours: U1, the ESP32-PICO-D4 (printed U?), and J3, the battery connector (printed Li_Ion). Nets the\nvendor left unnamed carry names of ours (ANT_FEED, AXP_LX1...). The MPU6886's pin names are its\ndatasheet's, shortened where it gives several (INT, FSYNC, RESV): the print numbers them only.\nThe CH552T's pin 10 is named P3.0, the datasheet's name (K15). Zones: columns 1-8 and rows A-F,\n50 mm apart, printed in the border."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 215.9 88.605 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.75 1.75)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6f53cdb2-3956-5898-a533-b245732a41d1")
	)
